(Introduction and Research) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(The Personal Budget Tracker emerged from research into the financial challenges faced by) Tj
0 -14 Td
(individuals who juggle multiple income sources and recurring expenses without a reliable) Tj
0 -14 Td
(way to monitor them. Informal surveys among peers and review of academic literature on) Tj
0 -14 Td
(financial literacy revealed that many people rely on ad‑hoc spreadsheets or simple) Tj
0 -14 Td
(notebook entries. While those methods provide a rudimentary overview, they fall short when) Tj
0 -14 Td
(categorizing transactions, generating summaries, or visualizing trends. Contemporary) Tj
0 -14 Td
(budgeting applications such as Mint, YNAB, and PocketGuard offer powerful functionality,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(yet they often require connecting to bank accounts, introduce recurring subscription) Tj
0 -14 Td
(costs, or present overwhelming interfaces for newcomers. The research phase therefore) Tj
0 -14 Td
(focused on bridging the gap between complex professional tools and minimal personal) Tj
0 -14 Td
(tracking methods. The goal was to design a lightweight, privacy‑respecting, and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(self‑hosted solution using open source technologies.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Throughout the research, emphasis was placed on accessibility and data ownership. By) Tj
0 -14 Td
(relying on local storage via SQLite and providing a simple Express.js server, the project) Tj
0 -14 Td
(ensures that users retain control over their financial records. Academic articles on) Tj
0 -14 Td
(personal finance management recommended clear categorization, regular review, and visual) Tj
0 -14 Td
(feedback as best practices for budgeting. These principles directly influenced the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(application's features. Moreover, the project studied usability heuristics to keep the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(interface approachable. Components like navigation layout, table listings, and form) Tj
0 -14 Td
(validation were inspired by common design patterns observed in well‑reviewed budgeting) Tj
0 -14 Td
(tools. This early research phase set a foundation for balancing functionality with) Tj
0 -14 Td
(simplicity, establishing the direction for subsequent development efforts.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Objectives) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(The project pursued several key objectives. First, it aimed to provide a straightforward) Tj
0 -14 Td
(interface where users can log income and expenses without the friction of creating) Tj
0 -14 Td
(accounts or connecting external services. Second, it sought to categorize each) Tj
0 -14 Td
(transaction, enabling meaningful aggregation and comparisons across types of spending.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Third, the tracker endeavored to compute and present real‑time summaries such as total) Tj
0 -14 Td
(income, total expenses, and the resulting net balance. A final objective was to) Tj
0 -14 Td
(incorporate visualizations that transform raw numbers into intuitive graphics, thereby) Tj
0 -14 Td
(reinforcing spending awareness.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Another vital objective centered on maintainability and extensibility. The codebase was) Tj
0 -14 Td
(structured so that future developers—or the original author at a later time—could easily) Tj
0 -14 Td
(add authentication, import/export features, or more advanced analytics. The use of popular) Tj
0 -14 Td
(libraries like Sequelize for database interactions and Nunjucks for templating reflects) Tj
0 -14 Td
(this forward‑looking mindset. The objectives also included adherence to security best) Tj
0 -14 Td
(practices, such as employing Helmet for HTTP headers and Morgan for detailed request) Tj
0 -14 Td
(logging. By meeting these objectives, the project would offer a reliable foundation for) Tj
0 -14 Td
(personal financial management while remaining accessible to learners who wish to explore) Tj
0 -14 Td
(full‑stack JavaScript development.) Tj
