(Sequelize and SQLite were chosen for their minimal configuration overhead. Two primary) Tj
0 -14 Td
(models—`Category` and `Transaction`—capture the core data entities. Each transaction) Tj
0 -14 Td
(stores an amount, date, description, type \(income or expense\), and associated category.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Relationships were defined so that categories have many transactions, and each transaction) Tj
0 -14 Td
(belongs to a single category. After initializing the database schema, the project) Tj
0 -14 Td
(implemented CRUD routes for transactions and categories. Routes handle operations such as) Tj
0 -14 Td
(listing transactions with optional filters, rendering forms for creation or editing, and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(performing deletion. Client input is validated at the model level by specifying non‑null) Tj
0 -14 Td
(constraints and enumeration of the transaction type.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(With data persistence in place, development progressed to computing aggregate summaries) Tj
0 -14 Td
(for the dashboard. The application calculates total income and total expenses using) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Sequelize's `sum` function and presents recent transactions in a concise table. A summary) Tj
0 -14 Td
(API endpoint provides grouped totals by category, returning JSON data consumed by a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Chart.js visualization. During development, nodemon facilitated rapid feedback,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(automatically restarting the server after changes. Middleware like body‑parser, Morgan,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and Helmet ensured robust request handling, logging, and basic security hardening. Each) Tj
0 -14 Td
(feature was iteratively tested through the browser interface, validating data retrieval,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(input handling, and user feedback messages.) Tj
